18:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg mb-6","children":"Six reasons ads convert to clicks but not sales"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Message Match"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"Ad promised X - landing page delivers Y"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"The ad copy set a specific expectation: a price point, a product type, a use case, a promotional offer. The landing page the visitor arrived at addresses a different angle or uses different language. The visitor cannot reconcile the two in under three seconds, so they leave. This is the single largest source of post-click abandonment in paid search. It is not about aesthetics - it is a literal mismatch between the claim that generated the click and the claim the page leads with."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Put the ad's primary promise - verbatim or near-verbatim - in the H1. If the ad says \"Free shipping on orders over $50,\" the page headline confirms it immediately. One ad group per landing page variant is the structural fix."}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap